# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# m68020 core (rtl/m68020_core.sv inside rtl/m68020_fx68k.sv, instance "cpu")
#
# Add to fx68k/constraints/base64.fdc AFTER removing every constraint and
# define_attribute that names cpu.excUnit.* or cpu.U_nanoRom_t3.* (fx68k cells
# that no longer exist -> BN105 warnings).
#
# Every flop inside cpu.core is clock-enabled every CE_DIV-th clk_12x. The
# wrapper registers on those same enable edges:
#   into the core : c_ack, c_berr, c_rdata, c_rst_n
#   out of it     : q_req, q_we, q_addr, q_wdata, q_size, q_fc (the request, for the
#                   68000 bus engine) and q_reset_out, q_halted (to the board)
# so every path between two of those (core <-> core, core -> q_*, c_* -> core)
# is a CE_DIV-cycle path. Everything else, including the enable itself (ce_q) and
# ipl_s into the core, is single-cycle and must stay that way.
# Values below are for CE_DIV = 3 (setup 3, hold 2). For CE_DIV = 4 use -setup 4 -hold 3.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
set_multicycle_path -setup 3 -hold 2 -from [get_cells {cpu.core.*}] -to [get_cells {cpu.core.*}]
set_multicycle_path -setup 3 -hold 2 -from [get_cells {cpu.c_ack* cpu.c_berr* cpu.c_rdata* cpu.c_rst_n*}] -to [get_cells {cpu.core.*}]
set_multicycle_path -setup 3 -hold 2 -from [get_cells {cpu.core.*}] -to [get_cells {cpu.q_*}]
